  "name": "spw-workbench",
  "description": "A research-oriented workbench for the Spw language ecosystem, facilitating the exploration of parsing and runtime behaviors across syntactic, semantic, and pragmatic interpretive layers. The platform employs a domain-driven architecture with signal-based reactivity and an ARIA-coupled UI system to enforce semantic coherence and accessibility. It integrates specialized tooling for lens algebra, operator calculus, and formal auditing of architectural invariants.",
